From: Stealth Build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 01/05] Hide navigator.webdriver at Blink level

Force the navigator.webdriver getter to return false so
`navigator.webdriver` is always false regardless of the
--enable-automation / AutomationControlled runtime state or any
DevTools automation override.

VERIFIED against tag 151.0.7922.108: in v151 the getter lives in
Navigator::webdriver() in core/frame/navigator.cc (the old
navigator_automation_information.cc/.h no longer exist -- only the .idl
remains and it binds to Navigator). We replace the whole body so there
is no unreachable/dead code (Chromium builds with -Werror).

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator.cc
@@ -100,7 +100,9 @@ bool Navigator::cookieEnabled() const {
 bool Navigator::webdriver() const {
-  if (RuntimeEnabledFeatures::AutomationControlledEnabled())
-    return true;
-
-  bool automation_enabled = false;
-  probe::ApplyAutomationOverride(GetExecutionContext(), automation_enabled);
-  return automation_enabled;
+  // Stealth: always report navigator.webdriver === false regardless of the
+  // --enable-automation / AutomationControlled runtime state.
+  return false;
 }
